 "HEADLINE": {
  "THE_VERDICT_NO_LONGER_FLIPS_ON_ONE_FRAME": {
   "pre_registered_as_the_bigger_finding_if_it_did": "it does not.",
   "N40_with_DSC_6239_INCLUDED": "axis constancy chi2 69.5 on 4 dof -> REJECTS; constancy fit chi2/dof 53.1 on 7 dof -> REJECTS.",
   "N40_with_it_excluded": "chi2 686.7 and 129.4 \u2014 same direction, ~10x stronger.",
   "so": "the 5-frame 'nothing rejects with all frames in' was a SMALL-SAMPLE ARTEFACT. One anomalous frame is 20% of five and 2.5% of forty; at N=40 it inflates the SEs ~3x (1.2-1.7 deg against 0.3-1.0) but no longer hides the effect. The gate failure STANDS without needing the exclusion.",
   "consequence": "corner-fix-landscape's rl -loadpsf= route remains failed, and the one-frame condition that had to travel with that verdict can now be DROPPED."
  },
  "Q3_DSC_6239_IS_UNIQUE_NOT_A_CLASS": {
   "question": "is 'first frame of a run' a class, which would make the exclusion a systematic everywhere it has been used?",
   "answer": "NO. Only the first frame of the SET is anomalous; the other four group-starts are ordinary.",
   "group_start_axes_deg": {
    "DSC_6239": -36.91,
    "DSC_6339": 16.84,
    "DSC_6439": 17.2,
    "DSC_6539": 17.5,
    "DSC_6639": 16.29
   },
   "reference_index_ge_25": {
    "mean_axis_deg": 17.39,
    "sd": 1.52,
    "n": 20
   },
   "group_starts_EXCLUDING_6239_vs_rest": "-0.44 +- 0.43 deg = 1.0 sigma \u2014 no class effect",
   "robust_z": "DSC_6239 sits at z = -25.7; the NEXT most deviant of 40 frames is -1.4. It is not the tail of a distribution, it is a different object.",
   "corroboration": "its fixed-term amplitude is 0.4661 against 0.69-0.83 for every other frame \u2014 the same signature the record already carries for it in two other quantities (0.4615 against 0.757-0.815; theta0 departing 19.75 deg)."
  },
  "A_CONSEQUENCE_FOR_A_GATED_TARGET": "psf_work/f{1,2,3}.lst \u2014 Gate 1A's 8074-star sample \u2014 is DSC_6239 / 6339 / 6439, i.e. the first frames of groups 1, 2 and 3. Only 6239 is anomalous, so ONE THIRD of that sample carries the anomaly. Gate 1A still reproduces its recorded numbers exactly (it is the same data), but anyone reading 0.5869 / 0.5798 as representative of the corpus should know its composition.",
  "SUBSET_BRACKET_EXACT": "restricted to the original five frames this reproduces constancy_fit.json to the digit \u2014 span 15.4 deg, axis chi2 3.0/4, fit chi2/dof 1.81, f 4.31 +- 1.80; and dropping 6239 from them gives 16.5 / 74.6 / 19.29 / 5.72 +- 0.53. The harness did not move.",
  "WHAT_THIS_DOES_NOT_SETTLE": "chi2/dof of 53-129 means the constancy model is BADLY misspecified, not that it has measured something: the best-fit f stays at ~3.6, about 4x the predicted trail, which is what a wrong model returns. And the named alternative in constancy_fit.json is untouched \u2014 an unmodelled rho-dependent demosaic term produces the same non-constancy, and the demosaic cannot be pinned from a script. 'No field-constant optical component' remains the leading reading, not the only one."
 }
